# Deterministic reviewer evidence.
#
# Every artefact under reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis binds its numbers to the
# SHA-256 of the bytes it was generated from -- the committed manifest.csv above all
# -- through the provenance records beside it. Those bytes must therefore be the same
# in every checkout. A fresh clone on a host whose core.autocrlf is true would
# otherwise check the CSV and JSON out with CRLF: manifest.csv would hash 2ff7c3f7...
# instead of 064a289b..., and every axis (WP1, resolution, burst and PRF) would
# refuse to run with a manifest-mismatch reason. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for
# exactly these paths; nothing else in the repository changes behaviour.
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/*.csv text eol=lf
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/*.json text eol=lf

# Committed figures are binary evidence: never translated, never diffed as text.
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/figures/*.png binary
